-- V1__init.sql — Phase 0 baseline migration (ADR-0005, ADR-0016).
--
-- Deliberately near-empty: its only job is to prove the Flyway pipe wires up and
-- runs on startup against real Postgres. Flyway still records it in
-- flyway_schema_history, which the Phase 0 acceptance test asserts.
--
-- Persistence baseline conventions established here for every later migration
-- to follow (ADR-0016):
--   * Primary keys are bigint identity: `id bigint GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY`.
--   * Audit timestamps (created_at / updated_at) are set app-side by Hibernate
--     (@CreationTimestamp / @UpdateTimestamp via base.AuditedEntity) — NOT by DB
--     triggers, and no created-by / modified-by columns.
--   * Money is numeric(19,2) (ADR-0010).
--
-- No extensions (pgcrypto, citext, …) are planted speculatively. Each feature
-- phase adds its own V2__…, V3__… migration for its tables.
